_meanings:
.²1 Making perfect, refining, polishing; ({#maRiH#}) {#prayuktasaMskAra ivADikaM#}
 {#baBO#} <ls>R. 3. 18</ls>.
.²2 Refinement, perfection, grammatical purity (as of words); {#saMskAravatyeva#}
 {#girA manIzI#} <ls>Ku. 1. 28</ls> (where <ls>Malli.</ls> renders the word by {#vyAkaraRajanyA#}
 {#SudDiH#}); <ls>R. 15. 76</ls>.
.²3 Education, cultivation, training (as of the mind); {#nisargasaMskAravinIta#}
 {#ityasO nfpeRa cakre yuvarAjaSabdaBAk#} <ls>R. 3. 35</ls>; <ls>Ku. 7. 10</ls>.
.²4 Making ready, preparation.
.²5 Cooking, dressing (as of food <ab>&c.</ab>).
.²6 Embellishment, decoration, ornament; {#svaBAvasundaraM vastu na saMskAramapekzate#}
 <ls>Dṛ. Ś. 49</ls>; <ls>Ś. 7. 23</ls>; <ls>Mu. 2. 10</ls>.
.²7 Consecration, sanctification, hallowing; {#saMskAro nAma sa Bavati#}
 {#yasmiYjAte padArTo Bavati yogyaH kasyacidarTasya#} <ls>ŚB. on MS. 3. 1. 3</ls>.
.²8 Impression, form, mould, operation, influence; {#yannave BAjane lagnaH#}
 {#saMskAro nAnyaTA Bavet#} <ls>H. Pr. 8</ls>; <ls>Bh. 3. 84</ls>.
.²9 Idea, notion, conception.
.²10 Any faculty or capacity.
.²11 Effect of work, merit of action; {#PalAnumeyAH prAramBAH saMskArAH#}
 {#prAktanA iva#} <ls>R. 1. 20</ls>.
.²12 The self-reproductive quality, faculty of impression; one of the 24 qualities

 or guṇas recognised by the Vaiśeṣikas; it is of three kinds: {#BAvanA#},
 {#vega#}, and {#sTitisTApakatA#} <ab>qq. vv.</ab>
.²13 The faculty of recollection, impression on the memory; {#saMskAramAtrajanyaM#}
 {#jYAnaM smftiH#} <ls>T. S.</ls>
.²14 A purificatory rite, a sacred rite or ceremony; {#saMskArArTaM SarIrasya#}
 <ls>Ms. 2. 66</ls>; <ls>R. 10. 78</ls>; (Manu mentions 12 such Saṃskāras <ab>viz.</ab> 1 {#garBADAna#},
 2 {#puMsavana#}, 3 {#sImantonnayana#}, 4 {#jAtakarman#}, 5 {#nAmakarman#},
 6 {#nizkramaRa#}, 7 {#annaprASana#}, 8 {#cUqAkarman#}, 9 {#upanayana#},
 10 {#keSAnta#}, 11 {#samAvartana#}, and 12 {#vivAha#}; see <ls>Ms. 2. 26</ls>
 <ab>&c.</ab>; some writers increase the number to sixteen).
.²15 Purification, purity.
.²16 A rite or ceremony in general.
.²17 Investiture with the sacred thread; {#mAMsaM mUtraM purIzaM ca prASya#}
 {#saMskAramarhati#} <ls>Mb. 12. 165. 76</ls>.
.²18 Obsequial ceremonies.
.²19 A polishing stone; {#saMskArolliKito mahAmaRiriva kzIRo'pi nAlakzyate#}
 <ls>Ś. 6. 5</ls> (where {#saMskAra#} may mean ‘polishing’ also).
